# join without on (DS0122); the right table is the last thing before the pipe.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | join u | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..20
  PIPELINE@0..19
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    JOIN_OP@4..10
      IDENT@4..8 "join"
      WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
      NAME_REF@9..10
        IDENT@9..10 "u"
    WHITESPACE@10..11 " "
    PIPE@11..12 "|"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    TAKE_OP@13..19
      IDENT@13..17 "take"
      WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
      LITERAL@18..19
        LONG@18..19 "1"
  WHITESPACE@19..20 "\n"

error[DS0122]: `join` needs `on` and the columns to match
  --> query:1:10
  |
1 | t | join u | take 1
  |          ^ expected `on` after this table
  |
  = help: say which columns to match: `join u on customerId`
